{
 "id": "2026-10-18-istanbul-floods-toll",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Five dead, thousands rescued. How much rain did Istanbul actually get?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Istanbul's governor says three thousand fifty people were rescued, and no one is still waiting for rescue. Daily Sabah reports that a missing person's body was found in the Golden Horn on Sunday. That brings the toll to five."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Turkey's interior minister said rainfall reached two hundred seventy-two kilograms per square meter in parts of the city. That equals two hundred seventy-two liters on every square meter. Officials call it the worst in more than eighty years."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Officials say several people are still missing, and counts differ between outlets. Turkey's weather service has issued orange alerts for Istanbul and four nearby provinces. Türkiye Today reports a second round of rain, and debris from the first floods is not fully cleared."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Istanbul avoid another deadly flood this autumn? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
